```{.r .cell-code}
library(dplyr)
library(ggplot2)
library(gt)
library(ggokabeito)   # color-blind-safe (Okabe-Ito) scale

data(penguins)
penguins <- penguins |> filter(!is.na(bill_len), !is.na(bill_dep))
```
:::


## The data

We measured **342** penguins of 3 species
(Adelie\, Chinstrap\, and Gentoo), collected at Palmer Station, Antarctica
[@gorman2014]. The data are available through the **palmerpenguins** package [@horst2020] and are now
also included in base R's `datasets` package.

The species are not evenly represented:


::: {.cell .column-margin}

```{.r .cell-code}
penguins |>
  count(species, name = "n") |>
  knitr::kable()
```

::: {.cell-output-display}


|species   |   n|
|:---------|---:|
|Adelie    | 151|
|Chinstrap |  68|
|Gentoo    | 123|


:::
:::


## Bill shape separates the species

@fig-bill shows that within a species the bill has a characteristic shape, so the species form
clusters.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
ggplot(penguins, aes(bill_len, bill_dep, color = species, shape = species)) +
  geom_point(alpha = 0.8) +
  scale_color_okabe_ito() +
  labs(x = "Bill length (mm)", y = "Bill depth (mm)", color = "Species", shape = "Species") +
  theme_minimal(base_size = 12)
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![Bill length versus depth, colored by species.](penguins-report_files/figure-html/fig-bill-1.png){#fig-bill fig-alt='Scatter plot of bill depth against bill length for penguins of three species, each drawn in a distinct color and shape. The three species form largely separate clusters.' width=480}
:::
:::


A compact descriptor of bill shape is the length-to-depth ratio (@eq-ratio):

$$
\text{ratio} = \frac{\text{bill\_len}}{\text{bill\_dep}}
$$ {#eq-ratio}

## Mean measurements

@tbl-summary reports the mean bill measurements and body mass per species.


::: {#tbl-summary .cell tbl-cap='Mean measurements per species.'}

```{.r .cell-code}
penguins |>
  summarise(
    n = n(),
    bill_len = mean(bill_len),
    bill_dep = mean(bill_dep),
    body_mass = mean(body_mass, na.rm = TRUE),
    .by = species
  ) |>
  gt() |>
  cols_label(species = "Species", n = "N", bill_len = "Bill length (mm)",
             bill_dep = "Bill depth (mm)", body_mass = "Body mass (g)") |>
  fmt_number(columns = c(bill_len, bill_dep), decimals = 1) |>
  fmt_number(columns = body_mass, decimals = 0)
```

